meta {
  name: start QR pairing
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/internal/rcs/pair/start
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Begins a QR pairing attempt. The page drives this for you; call it directly
  only if you are scripting.

  It takes a few seconds, because it fetches Google config and opens a login
  session before it can produce a code.

  Then fetch `QR code` and scan it. The code is regenerated every 30 seconds
  server-side for up to 10 minutes, after which the attempt gives up.

  Only one attempt runs at a time, and it lives in the memory of the server process
  that served this request. Every following request must reach the same process.

  Errors:
  - 400 — an attempt is already running, or Google refused to start one
}
